 "Mark the correct statements about auscultation in pulmonary oedema.",
 ["Early — crepitation and fine crackles at the bases", "Severe — medium and coarse crackles over the whole lung", "Coarse crackles may be heard at a distance like a “boiling samovar”", "How high the crackles reach shows the severity", "Only wheezes are heard", "Crackles are heard only over the apices", "Amphoric breathing is the main sign", "A pleural rub is always heard"],
 "Xirillashlar sathi kurak burchagigacha bo‘lsa — o‘rtacha, butun o‘pka bo‘ylab — og‘ir shish; bu davo samarasini kuzatishda qulay.",
